{"type": "message", "id": "e8dc572a", "parentId": "9437744a", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T16:00:14.362Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "tool-c32b17eb85b44a748867749f60db9c8e", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"NAEP 2022 grade 8 math scores all states table ranking Arizona Kansas Kentucky\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1002,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4cb3cc3354faec85\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4cb3cc3354faec85\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3f048e377570709a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe table below shows the number of states/jurisdictions with score increases or decreases in 2022 and how many states/jurisdictions scored higher, lower, or not significantly different than the nation (public) in NAEP mathematics.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3f048e377570709a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"429708fc7ff1098e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP scores by state - Ballotpedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"429708fc7ff1098e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ballotpedia.org/NAEP_scores_by_state\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"67f13a9381f79a38\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe table below details math and reading scores for students in fourth grade and eighth grade using the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP). All 50 states and Washington, D.C.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"67f13a9381f79a38\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ballotpedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"320fc0ed4fc2f3a4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"320fc0ed4fc2f3a4\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3c71a179f0bc4421\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, <strong>female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3c71a179f0bc4421\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"70e2471d62b31a64\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"70e2471d62b31a64\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"25e386345943b4a3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP ACHIEVEMENT-LEVEL PERCENTAGES AND AVERAGE SCORE\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"25e386345943b4a3\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"147771d2c0d655d5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe New NAEP Scores Highlight a Standards Gap in Many States - FutureEd\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"147771d2c0d655d5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.future-ed.org/the-new-naep-scores-highlight-a-standards-gap-in-many-states/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9a2f7c971e55bd6a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nForty-seven states improved NAEP math proficiency rates between 2022 and 2024 in fourth grade and 36 states did so in eighth grade. But proficiency rates remain below 2019 levels in 34 states in fourth-grade and in all but one state in eighth-grade. Similarly, math proficiency rates rose on nearly every state’s standardized tests during the same period. While state math scores declined dramatically between 2019 and 2022, particularly in eighth grade, only in Arizona, Arkansas, Florida, Idaho, and Vermont in fourth grade and Arkansas, Michigan, and Missouri in eighth grade did state test scores decline between 2022 and 2024.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9a2f7c971e55bd6a\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 10, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.future-ed.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "NAEP 2022 grade 8 math scores all states table ranking Arizona Kansas Kentucky", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 1002, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4cb3cc3354faec85\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4cb3cc3354faec85\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3f048e377570709a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe table below shows the number of states/jurisdictions with score increases or decreases in 2022 and how many states/jurisdictions scored higher, lower, or not significantly different than the nation (public) in NAEP mathematics.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3f048e377570709a\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"429708fc7ff1098e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP scores by state - Ballotpedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"429708fc7ff1098e\">>>", "url": "https://ballotpedia.org/NAEP_scores_by_state", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"67f13a9381f79a38\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe table below details math and reading scores for students in fourth grade and eighth grade using the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP). All 50 states and Washington, D.C.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"67f13a9381f79a38\">>>", "siteName": "ballotpedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"320fc0ed4fc2f3a4\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"320fc0ed4fc2f3a4\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3c71a179f0bc4421\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, <strong>female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3c71a179f0bc4421\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"70e2471d62b31a64\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"70e2471d62b31a64\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"25e386345943b4a3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP ACHIEVEMENT-LEVEL PERCENTAGES AND AVERAGE SCORE\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"25e386345943b4a3\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"147771d2c0d655d5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe New NAEP Scores Highlight a Standards Gap in Many States - FutureEd\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"147771d2c0d655d5\">>>", "url": "https://www.future-ed.org/the-new-naep-scores-highlight-a-standards-gap-in-many-states/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9a2f7c971e55bd6a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nForty-seven states improved NAEP math proficiency rates between 2022 and 2024 in fourth grade and 36 states did so in eighth grade. But proficiency rates remain below 2019 levels in 34 states in fourth-grade and in all but one state in eighth-grade. Similarly, math proficiency rates rose on nearly every state’s standardized tests during the same period. While state math scores declined dramatically between 2019 and 2022, particularly in eighth grade, only in Arizona, Arkansas, Florida, Idaho, and Vermont in fourth grade and Arkansas, Michigan, and Missouri in eighth grade did state test scores decline between 2022 and 2024.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9a2f7c971e55bd6a\">>>", "published": "February 10, 2025", "siteName": "www.future-ed.org"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1776355214361}}
